Keep an already-running adb server that reports version 31 instead of killing it.

adb refuses to talk to a server whose version differs from its own
(ADB_SERVER_VERSION, 41 here): it prints a mismatch warning, kills the server
and starts its own. Version 31 speaks the same wire protocol, so the restart
is unnecessary and throws away the server that was already serving devices.

--- a/vendor/adb/client/adb_client.cpp
+++ b/vendor/adb/client/adb_client.cpp
@@ -308,7 +308,9 @@
             }
         }
 
-        if (version != ADB_SERVER_VERSION) {
+        // Accept the older server version 31 as well. It speaks the same wire
+        // protocol, so there is no need to kill it just because it is older.
+        if (version != ADB_SERVER_VERSION && version != 31) {
 #if defined(__linux__)
             if (version > ADB_SERVER_VERSION && local) {
                 // Try to re-exec the existing adb server's binary.
